===Find the "surreal" part of this memory{{subst:void|<!--202050301-->}}===
{{Mission Description|type=companion|location=Memory-Belobog|People usually think about blizzards and freezing temperatures when it comes to Belobog, but the most profound memory March 7th have of that place is the impressive lobby of the Goethe Hotel.<br />She claims it is because she became a wanted criminal the day after she checked into the hotel. However... perhaps it is because a bright yet brief campfire is more memorable than even an epic in the dead of winter, no matter how magnificent the journey was.}}
{{Dialogue Start}}
----
:'''March 7th:''' What the actual &mdash; that thing was flaming hot! You said things that never happened to me in reality couldn't happen here!
:'''Fu Xuan:''' I said that if something hasn't injured you in reality, then it cannot injure you in memory..... I didn't say anything about the sensation of injury.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' So this is Belobog? I was expecting it to be cold.
:'''March 7th:''' It's freezing... Huh? Master Diviner, aren't you cold? I can't stop shivering.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' Hmm, most likely a result of me never having experienced true cold. I'm afraid you'll have to do the shivering by yourself.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' On the Luofu, you and I have shared experiences, and so I was able to provide more active assistance... but in Belobog, you'll have to rely on your own judgment to ascertain the source of distortion and get the foreign object to appear.
:'''March 7th:''' Yeah, yeah, I get it.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' Oh, Miss March, I have one more thing to ask... Have you ever experienced great suffering?
:'''March 7th:''' Huh? I don't think so. Why are you suddenly asking me that?
:'''Fu Xuan:''' Sometimes people forget extreme memories to protect themselves from suffering...
:'''Fu Xuan:''' Perhaps you didn't notice, but in your memories of the Luofu, everyone you met was either hinting or explicitly stating that you should stop trying to remember.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' I believe this is most likely your subconscious communicating with you directly... though of course, we cannot rule out that external forces may have interfered with your memory. In the latter case, it is possible that someone decided to leave warnings in your subconscious to prevent you from recalling the truth.
:'''March 7th:''' Am I really that important to someone...? I don't think there's anyone who'd go to all the trouble of locking up my memories...
:'''Fu Xuan:''' ...And yet, memories are precisely what you seek, no?
:'''March 7th:''' Hmm...
:'''Fu Xuan:''' I say this to say one thing &mdash; are you certain you wish to continue exploring your memories?
:'''March 7th:''' You said external forces might be messing with my head, right? That just makes me more curious. Hmph, no one gets away with locking up MY memories! Let's go. I'll show you the way to Goethe Hotel!
:'''Fu Xuan:''' Hehe, very well. I must admit that I'm finding the whole matter more interesting by the minute.
----
:'''March 7th:''' This memory should be from the first day we arrived in Belobog. By the second day, we were wanted criminals already...
:'''March 7th:''' "The person present, who shouldn't be"... Who could it be?

;(Talk to Sampo)
:'''Memory-Sampo:''' Miss March, long time no see! Welcome to the Sampo Hotel!
:'''March 7th:''' ...Th&mdash;The Sampo Hotel? This is Goethe Hotel!
:'''Memory-Sampo:''' WAS Goethe Hotel, hehe &mdash; now it's the Sampo Hotel! In the autumn of his years, Old Goethe got too old to run this place &mdash; so he handed it down to his most trusted young confidant &mdash; Sampo Koski!
:'''Memory-Sampo:''' And before you get the wrong idea, there was ZERO trickery involved &mdash; this was a cherished agreement between gentlemen.
:'''Memory-Sampo:''' You see, Old Goethe and I chose to face the future instead of clinging to memories of the past... you should do the same, March.
:'''Fu Xuan:''' This blue-haired fellow has an air of deceit about him every time he opens his mouth.
:'''March 7th:''' Haha, you don't need a jade abacus to get a feel for Sampo...
